  "storedDescription": "Saved (past) workout badge cases, run by Android StoredWorkoutPersonalRecordsTest and iOS PersonalRecordsGoldenTests. history entries carry 'when' relative to the viewed workout: earlier (older date), same-date-lower-id and same-date-higher-id (same date, tie-broken by workout id: only lower ids are earlier), later (newer date), self (the viewed workout itself). Only earlier workouts form the baseline. workout lists exercise blocks in order and a repeated exercise key is a second block of the same exercise: the running best carries across its blocks. Every set is compared with the better of the earlier-history best and the sets before it; expected.records is one flag per set per block. Same rules as the live cases: no earlier history means no record, 0 kg is never a record, equal to the best is not a record, weight or estimated one-rep max can each make a record.",
  "storedCases": [
    {
      "id": "stored-first-ever-workout",
      "description": "The first workout of an exercise has no earlier history, so no set is a record.",
      "history": [],
      "workout": [
        {
          "exercise": "bench",
          "sets": [
            {
              "weight": 60,
              "reps": 8
            },
            {
              "weight": 100,
              "reps": 5
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "expected": {
        "records": [
          {
            "exercise": "bench",
            "sets": [
              false,
              false
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "stored-later-and-self-history-ignored",
      "description": "Newer workouts and the viewed workout itself are not baseline, so without older history there is no record.",
